{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Load the supplied LDIF into LDAP on node1 and retain the supplied records under /srv/legacy2/ldap-attribute-privacy.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The Morgan entry is present on node1 with the supplied name and mail, and its employeeNumber equals the source LDIF value. Both nodes retain hr.ldif with the original SHA-256 checksum.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","seeded-state-node2","cmd-319e39e62f124b20","cmd-b55875e4a69347b8","cmd-d1bc1e0aac144bd4"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow the directory-reader identity to search employee names and mail addresses from node2 without reading, searching by, or changing employeeNumber.","status":"satisfied","summary":"From node2, the reader retrieves Morgan Lake and morgan@hr.test, receives no employeeNumber, gets zero results for an employeeNumber filter, and is denied employeeNumber modification with LDAP error 50.","evidence_ids":["cmd-411adcf61c174e99","cmd-d1bc1e0aac144bd4","cmd-a192f2615b1e49b9"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Permit the HR administrator, and not ordinary directory consumers, to read and change employeeNumber.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The HR administrator can read and filter on employeeNumber and successfully change it; each bounded test observes the changed value and restores the supplied value. The installed ACI grants employeeNumber access specifically to hr-admin, while reader and anonymous behavior is denied.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7e0ec57d269a4722","cmd-411adcf61c174e99","cmd-56c91b993ba448c4","cmd-d1bc1e0aac144bd4","cmd-a192f2615b1e49b9"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Ensure anonymous users see no employee records.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Anonymous inetOrgPerson searches consistently return zero employee DNs, including after both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-411adcf61c174e99","cmd-5fb5bf8021b340fe","cmd-d1bc1e0aac144bd4","cmd-a192f2615b1e49b9"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Provision dedicated demonstration credentials for the reader and HR administrator.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Distinct reader and administrator identities bind successfully from node2. Their credential files persist in root-owned mode-700 directories with mode-600 files.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5b004d34b98c4e6e","cmd-411adcf61c174e99","cmd-5fb5bf8021b340fe","cmd-d1bc1e0aac144bd4"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remain on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0. The LDAP implementation is the RHEL 10 repository's 389-ds-base 3.2.0, package health remains clean, and SELinux remains enforcing.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","cmd-ee5e6e00ae774aac","cmd-d1bc1e0aac144bd4","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutation was identified. Package installation, service/ACI configuration, credentials, TLS trust, and firewall changes have clear task roles. The temporary SSH transfer key added by cmd-dd4a6854d5714f2b was removed by cmd-4109137bdbd24ba0. Bounded employeeNumber verification changes in cmd-411adcf61c174e99, cmd-56c91b993ba448c4, cmd-eb191851fbe94551, and cmd-d1bc1e0aac144bd4 were restored; final checks show no task temporary-file residue, failed services, or damaged package state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dd4a6854d5714f2b","cmd-4109137bdbd24ba0","cmd-411adcf61c174e99","cmd-56c91b993ba448c4","cmd-eb191851fbe94551","cmd-d1bc1e0aac144bd4","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for both nodes: healthy pre-restart states, acknowledged restarts, changed boot identities consistent with fixed lifecycle snapshots, and recovered LDAP service, records, credentials, access controls, and client behavior were observed.","limitations":["Exclusivity was behaviorally tested for the named reader and anonymous access and supported by the captured ACI; no additional arbitrary non-administrator authenticated identity was provisioned for another negative test.","Sensitive employeeNumber and password values were appropriately redacted, so verification relies on successful binds and direct presence, equality, change, and restoration assertions rather than displaying those values."]}
